A code compliance inspection is required to meet current requirements of the mandatory Georgia State Minimum Standard Codes and Optional Codes as adopted by the City of LaFayette, Georgia, upon the occurrence of one (1) of the following:
(1) Sale or conveyance of the subject property;
(2) Electricity to subject property has been turned off for a continuous twelve-month period;
(3) Finding of a code violation by the electric or codes department;
(4) Finding of a code violation under the existing building code;
(5) Finding of a violation under the property maintenance code;
(6) Following any fire;
(7) Upon a change of occupancy (use); or
(8) Finding a manifestly unsafe condition.
